                "coreConcept": "Refractory Hypoxemia (ARDS)",
                "caseSummary": "Patient with pneumonia developing ARDS. Key indicator is dropping SpO2 (92% -> 88% -> 85%) despite increasing oxygen support (2L -> 4L -> Non-Rebreather).",
                "answerAnalysis": "The hallmark of ARDS is refractory hypoxemia (hypoxia that does not improve with O2). The trend shows specific deterioration: HR rising (compensation), RR rising (air hunger), and O2 falling despite maximum non-invasive support.",
                "trap": "Assuming the PaCO2 of 30 (Alkalosis) is good. In early ARDS, patients hyperventilate, blowing off CO2. This is a sign of distress, not stability.",
