                "caseSummary": "Asthma exacerbation progressing to fatigue. The key trend is the **drop in Respiratory Rate** (38 -> 10) combined with **Rising CO2** (55).",
                "answerAnalysis": "Students generally associate 'lower RR' with improvement. In status asthmaticus, a sudden drop from tachypnea (38) to bradypnea (10) signals muscle fatigue and impending occurance. The 'Silent Chest' phenomenon occurs when airflow is so restricted that wheezing stops.",
